      "kind": "sign",
      "x": 11,
      "y": 16,
      "text": [
        "PROVISIONER - vessels, tonics, rope, boot wax.",
        "Open when the bells go, shut when the bells go."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "sign",
      "x": 20,
      "y": 10,
      "text": [
        "THE BELL HALL",
        "Verdant and Beast. Hallkeeper Tove Alder.",
        "Challengers welcome. Bring something other than a big stick."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "sign",
      "x": 18,
      "y": 23,
      "text": [
        "THE BELL TREE",
        "Older than the town. The town is named for it, not the other way round.",
        "Six bells. Do not add a seventh. People have tried."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "sign",
      "x": 2,
      "y": 19,
      "text": [
        "MARKET - Sixth day, dawn to bells.",
        "Today is not the sixth day. They are here anyway."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "sign",
      "x": 2,
      "y": 25,
      "text": [
        "THE GLASSHOUSE - seed stock for the whole valley.",
        "Mind the door. It sticks, and it is worth more than you are."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "sign",
      "x": 10,
      "y": 29,
      "text": [
        "THE BELL AND BARROW. Beds, board, and a fire that is always too hot."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "sign",
      "x": 16,
      "y": 34,
      "text": [
        "BRIARBELL",
        "Kin Clinic and market west. The Hall is under the tree. You cannot miss the tree."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "sign",
      "x": 22,
      "y": 22,
      "text": [
        "Bark like rope, and a hollow at the foot big enough to sit in.",
        "Somebody has been sitting in it. There is a cushion, and it is dry."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "sign",
      "x": 20,
      "y": 19,
      "text": [
        "A bell the size of a bucket, green with age, on a rope as thick as your wrist.",
        "The rim is worn bright where four hundred years of hands have steadied it."
      ]
    },
